==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|ragged}}, from {{etyl|gmq|en}}. Compare with Old Norse {{m|non|rǫgvathr||tufted}} and Norwegian {{m|no|ragget||shaggy}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|răg'ĭd}}, {{IPA|/ˈɹæɡɪd/|lang=en}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# In [[tatter]]s, having the texture broken.
#: ''a '''ragged''' coat''
#: ''a '''ragged''' sail''
# Having rough edges; [[jagged]] or [[uneven]]
#: '''''ragged''' rocks''
# Harsh-sounding; having an unpleasant noise
#* '''1912''', David Herbert Lawrence, ''The Trespasser'', Chapter 12
#*: There was a '''ragged''' noise of bleating from the flock penned in a corner of the yard. Two red-armed men seized a sheep, hauled it to a large bath that stood in the middle of the yard, and there held it, more or less in the bath, whilst a third man baled a dirty yellow liquid over its body.
# Wearing [[tattered]] clothes.
#: ''a '''ragged''' fellow''
# Rough; [[shaggy]]; [[rugged]].
# [[faulty|Faulty]]; lacking in [[skill]], [[reliability]], or [[organization]].
#* {{quote-book|title=Alice Nielsen and the Gayety of Nations|author=Dall Wilson|year=2010|page=318|ISBN=0557473675|passage=Now I realize how ridiculous and almost impertinent it was to expect New Yorkers to accept such a '''ragged''' performance for they have always demanded the best and do not tolerate the second-rate."}}
#* {{quote-journal
|date=May 19, 2012
|author=Paul fletcher
|title=Blackpool 1-2 West Ham
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/18044378
|page=
|passage=Allardyce's side had led at the break through a Carlton Cole strike but after Thomas Ince - son of former Hammers midfielder Paul - levelled shortly after the restart, the match became increasingly stretched and '''ragged'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Defense Manpower Planning: Issues for the 1980s|author=William J. Taylor, ‎Eric T. Olson, & ‎Richard A. Schrader|year=2013|page=219|ISBN=1483182347|passage=Despite the apparent general viability of the AVF its '''ragged''' performance serves to motivate serious questions concerning its future viability, the quality of the defense that we are buying, and the AVF's effect on our nation and society.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} performed in a [[syncopated]] manner, especially in [[ragtime]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} Of a [[data structure]]: having [[uneven]] [[level]]s.
#: ''a '''ragged''' hierarchy''
#: ''a '''ragged''' [[array]], consisting of a number of arrays of varying size''

